1
00:00:00,800 --> 00:00:04,267
This is Zukai — build cloud diagrams with AI.

2
00:00:04,267 --> 00:00:09,660
A free, open source diagram editor that runs entirely in your browser.

3
00:00:11,010 --> 00:00:12,853
No sign-up, no install.

4
00:00:12,853 --> 00:00:15,418
Open the page and start drawing.

5
00:00:15,418 --> 00:00:22,630
Cloud architecture, mind maps, sequence diagrams — every sample loads with a single click.

6
00:00:23,880 --> 00:00:28,097
AWS, Azure, Google Cloud and Lucide line icons are built in.

7
00:00:28,097 --> 00:00:33,860
Pick one from the left panel and the official icon drops straight onto the canvas.

8
00:00:35,110 --> 00:00:39,048
Drag to create a shape, then drag to connect it.

9
00:00:39,048 --> 00:00:47,170
Arrowheads, anchor points and orthogonal routing are all adjustable, on a canvas up to 4096 × 4096.

10
00:00:48,570 --> 00:00:52,304
Your diagram is saved as plain JSON — a .

11
00:00:52,304 --> 00:00:53,033
zu file.

12
00:00:53,033 --> 00:00:57,587
Readable by humans and by AI, and diffable in Git.

13
00:00:57,587 --> 00:01:02,870
Export to SVG or PDF, or copy the SVG straight into Figma.

14
00:01:04,120 --> 00:01:05,858
And then, AI editing.

15
00:01:05,858 --> 00:01:15,626
Paste your own API key into the built-in Claude or OpenAI panel, and simply describe the change: “Make the VPN band 1.

16
00:01:15,626 --> 00:01:16,453
2× taller.

17
00:01:16,453 --> 00:01:17,861
” Just like that.

18
00:01:17,861 --> 00:01:21,420
You can also drive it from Cursor over MCP.

19
00:01:22,720 --> 00:01:23,423
Zukai.

20
00:01:23,423 --> 00:01:26,940
Free, open source, no sign-up.

21
00:01:26,940 --> 00:01:30,340
Try it in your browser today.
